1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Thirteen atoms just simulated particles snapping into new pairs

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Pull confined particles apart and they make new pairs

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Physicists call it string breaking. Think quarks, as an analogy

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
13 ytterbium ions, held in a line

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Pairs formed at the ends of the string

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
And spread inward, not evenly along the string

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
A simulation of a lattice model. No real quarks, no real vacuum

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:35,000
De and Monroe, Duke Quantum Center
